Z||000000||GT Bastard||10-06-1999||04:52 PM||||I recently changed the shocks and struts in my 87 GT and it made a really great improvement.  The car handles so much better that I'm changing her name to "Stiffy".  Whadya think?  Nahhhh....  Anyhow, I highly recommend the Monroe Roadhandler shocks/struts.  They were only a few bucks more than the cheapies, and I got them at Advance Auto Parts for 17.99ea, and 44.00ea for the struts.  The job really wasn't all that bad, it just takes a little time.  The shocks were a breeze, and the struts took about an hour, not including the fact that I had to take the springs and struts to a Firestone to have the spring compressed and mated to the strut.  I took it to have it aligned afterwords too, of course.  All in all, it's well worth the effort.   <BR>later kiddies...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
